  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer anti-reflection coating on a silicon substrate. Incident medium is air. Incidence angle is 0 degrees. Polarization is unpolarized. The stack topology is exactly: air | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | silicon_substrate (8 dielectric layers total, alternating SiO2 (Lemarchand) and Ta2O5 (Gao), starting with SiO2 (Lemarchand) on the air side). Optimize the 8 individual layer thicknesses to minimize average reflectance across two wavelength bands simultaneously: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Each layer thickness must be between 20 nm and 400 nm. Materials are SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), and Si (substrate only). Report the optimized thicknesses, the average reflectance in each band, and the transmittance into the silicon substrate. The objective is to balance performance between the two bands rather than minimizing one at the expense of the other.",
